<div id="sky"></div>
<svg id="mountains" viewBox="0 0 1000 300" preserveAspectRatio="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <polygon points="0,300 0,190 120,110 230,175 340,90 460,180 560,120 680,200 800,130 900,190 1000,150 1000,300" fill="#9FB7CC" opacity=".55"/>
  <polygon points="0,300 0,230 100,170 210,220 330,150 440,215 540,165 650,225 760,175 880,230 1000,190 1000,300" fill="#6E88A2" opacity=".65"/>
</svg>
<canvas id="snowCanvas"></canvas>
<div id="aurora"></div>

<div class="wrap" id="pageWrap">

  <div class="brand">
    <div class="mark"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
    <div>
      <h1>Snowball</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Bury your debt, one throw at a time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="forecast" id="forecast">❄️ Forecast: —</div>

  <div class="hero">
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-label">Total remaining</div>
      <div class="stat-value" id="statTotal">£0</div>
      <div class="stat-sub" id="statTotalSub">across 0 debts</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-label">Snowballs ready</div>
      <div class="stat-value ember" id="statCharges">0</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">1 per £5 paid</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-label">Interest saved</div>
      <div class="stat-value gold" id="statSaved">£0.00</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">from early throws</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-label">Debts crushed</div>
      <div class="stat-value mint" id="statCrushed">0</div>
      <div class="stat-sub" id="statCrushedSub">keep going</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="setup-panel">
    <h3>Build your own snowball</h3>
    <p class="hint">This starts with example debts so you can see how it works. Add your own below — balance, interest rate and years remaining — and your line re-sorts smallest to largest automatically.</p>
    <div class="setup-grid">
      <div class="field"><label for="inName">Debt name</label><input type="text" id="inName" placeholder="e.g. Credit Card"></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="inBalance">Balance (£)</label><input type="number" id="inBalance" min="1" step="1" placeholder="1200"></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="inRate">Interest rate (APR %)</label><input type="number" id="inRate" min="0" step="0.1" placeholder="22.9"></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="inTerm">Years remaining</label><input type="number" id="inTerm" min="1" step="1" placeholder="24"></div>
      <button class="add-btn" id="addDebtBtn">+ Add debt</button>
    </div>
    <div class="setup-foot">
      <span class="demo-tag" id="demoTag">Showing example debts</span>
      <button class="clear-link" id="clearBtn">Clear everything &amp; start fresh</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Your snowball line</h2>
    <p>Smallest → largest</p>
  </div>
  <div class="line" id="debtLine"></div>

  <div class="actions">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Log a payment</h3>
      <p class="hint">Every £5 you log earns one snowball to throw.</p>
      <label for="debtSelect">Which debt</label>
      <select id="debtSelect"></select>
      <label for="amountInput">Amount paid (£)</label>
      <input type="number" id="amountInput" min="1" step="1" placeholder="e.g. 25">
      <button class="log-btn" id="logBtn">Log payment</button>
    </div>

    <div class="panel pile-area">
      <div class="pile-count" id="pileCount">0</div>
      <div class="pile-caption">snowballs packed and ready<br>tap "Throw" on any debt above</div>
      <div class="pile-icons" id="pileIcons"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer>
    <b>Prototype note:</b> "interest saved" is an estimate — chip amount × monthly rate × years remaining on that debt — a simplified stand-in for a full amortization schedule, close enough to feel rewarding without pretending to be financial advice. The sky, snowfall and each iceberg's cracks are driven by your real numbers. Everything here lives in memory for the preview; the real build would keep this in on-device storage plus an export/import backup file.
  </footer>

</div>

